course: dictionary
lesson: 2996
title: Words that hurt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are old-fashioned, and some are unkind. Dunce is both. Its meaning is a person who is slow to learn or thought to be stupid. Look at the clue in the sentence: «Do you take me for a dunce?» The speaker is asking if you think they are stupid, so the word is an insult.
explain: Look at the words around dunce to see how it is used. A dunce's cap was a tall paper cone hat that pupils in old schools were made to wear as a punishment. You can see the unkind feeling in the word itself: it is used to put someone down.
explain: Dunce is an old word, and today it is seen as cruel. Everyone learns at a different speed. A pupil who finds a lesson hard is not a dunce, and calling someone one is unkind. When you meet a word like this, ask: what would the speaker be trying to say about the other person?
fact: A dunce is a person who is slow to learn or thought to be stupid.
fact: A dunce's cap was a tall paper cone hat that old-fashioned schools used as a punishment.
fact: Dunce is old-fashioned and unkind, so it is not a nice word to use about someone.
fact: The word dunce comes from John Duns Scotus, a clever medieval thinker.
fact: His followers were later mocked as «Dunsmen», and the name became the word dunce.
exercise: «Do you take me for a dunce?» What does dunce mean here? | *A person thought to be stupid | A tall paper hat | A friendly teacher | A famous clever thinker
exercise: What is a dunce's cap? | A crown for the best pupil | A woolly hat for winter | *A tall paper cone hat pupils once wore as a punishment | A school bag
exercise: Why is calling someone a dunce unkind? | Because dunce is a long word | It means the same as clever | Because dunces are always happy | *Everyone learns at a different speed
test: Which word is closest in meaning to dunce? | Genius | Scholar | *Blockhead | Champion
test: Why should you avoid calling a classmate a dunce? | It is only used in France | *It is unkind and can hurt their feelings | It means the classmate is very tall | Dunce is the name of a sports team
exam: Ben got every answer right, so why is it wrong to call him a dunce? | *It is unkind, and it is not true of him | It is cruel and not true | Dunces are always tall | It means he is the best in the class
